---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', url: '/en/' },  { label: 'About', url: '/en/about/' }
];

const siteUrl = "https://www.petaginghub.com";
const hrefLangAlternates = [
  { lang: 'zh-TW', url: siteUrl + '/about' },
  { lang: 'en', url: siteUrl + '/en/about' },
  { lang: 'x-default', url: siteUrl + '/about' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us - Pet Aging Hub"
  description="Learn about Pet Aging Hub's mission to help pet owners better understand and care for their aging dogs and cats through educational tools and informational guides."
  lang="en"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hrefLangAlternates={hrefLangAlternates}>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">About Pet Aging Hub</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600">Helping pet owners understand aging and become better caregivers</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-slate prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Pet Aging Hub was founded in 2024 as a free online resource platform focused on pet aging and senior care. We believe every pet owner deserves access to practical, reliable information to help their senior pets live comfortable, healthy golden years.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">Our Mission</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Our mission is to <strong>translate complex veterinary knowledge into clear, actionable information</strong>. Through calculators, guide articles, and observation checklists, we help pet owners:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700 mb-6">
        <li>Understand their pet's life stage and aging progress</li>
        <li>Recognize health warning signs in senior pets</li>
        <li>Explore general breed and size context, not an individual care prescription</li>
        <li>Have more informed conversations with their veterinarian</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">What We Are Not</h2>
      <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-400 p-6 rounded-r-xl mb-6">
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Important: we are not a veterinary clinic and do not provide veterinary diagnoses or treatment recommendations.</strong> Our goal is to serve as a bridge between pet owners and professional veterinarians, not to replace professional veterinary care. All information and tools are for educational reference only and should not be the sole basis for medical decisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">What We Offer</h2>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mb-8">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="text-3xl">🧮</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Age Calculators</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">Our age calculators use Pet Aging Hub educational approximations, not official veterinary conversion formulas or biological-age measurements. Dog estimates use adult-size context; cat estimates use chronological age. These references cannot assess an individual pet’s health or lifespan.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="text-3xl">📚</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Educational Guide Articles</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Content covers aging, nutrition and everyday care, citing veterinary guidance or research where applicable and separating published information from site assumptions. Citations do not imply institutional endorsement or direct research validation of every page.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="text-3xl">📋</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Health Checklist Tools</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Our symptom checklists help pet owners assess whether their pet is showing health signs that need attention. These tools are not diagnostic systems or validated health scores. Selecting no symptoms cannot exclude illness; emergency warning signs should not wait for a website response.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="text-3xl">📊</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Breed &amp; Aging Data</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Different dog and cat breeds have different aging rates and life expectancy. The site’s breed and age references simplify real variation. General ranges and population findings cannot predict an individual pet’s lifespan. Some existing ranges are site-derived educational assumptions or general references, not validated predictions of an individual pet’s lifespan.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">Our Position</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Pet Aging Hub is an educational information website, not a veterinary clinic, diagnostic service or medical provider. The site name identifies the publisher, not a veterinary credential; this page does not claim veterinary authorship or review.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The site includes Google AdSense advertising. Advertisements are not evidence for an article or an endorsement of advertised products by veterinarians or professional organizations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">Sources and Content Maintenance</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        When interpreting sources, prioritize peer-reviewed primary research, formal veterinary guidelines and professional organizations, and reputable academic or veterinary institutions; site assumptions without direct support should be identified separately. Study populations, statistics and scope limit conclusions. Background sources do not validate a calculator model.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700 mb-6">
        <li>Treat our content as a starting reference point, not a final answer</li>
        <li>Discuss specific health concerns with a veterinarian familiar with your pet's history</li>
        <li>Material content or sourcing issues identified during maintenance are reviewed and corrected; not every page is continuously updated, and publication or update labels are not veterinary review dates</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">Contact Us</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        For a factual or sourcing issue, include the page URL, specific wording and a source that can be checked, using the <a href="/en/disclaimer/#contact-email" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">existing email contact method</a>. This is not urgent veterinary advice; response times and acceptance of suggested changes are not guaranteed. Do not send sensitive health or personal information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
